      "section_2_excerpt": "## 2. Risk-adaptive routing\n\nUse `policies/v4.8.0/workflow-routing.md` to classify the task and route it:\n\n- QUICK: Planner → deterministic Handoff → Implementer. Skip separate reviews by default.\n- STANDARD: Planner → independent Plan Review when the Plan requires it → deterministic Handoff → Implementer. Add Acceptance only when risk or a required gate calls for it.\n- CRITICAL: Planner → independent Plan Review → deterministic Handoff → Implementer → independent Acceptance.\n\nCritical means real security/privacy, data loss or migration, public compatibility, production, or consequential semantic risk. Do not classify routine reversible work as Critical by default. The user may pass a role's reviewed artifact to the next role; that handoff is not a new authorization gate. `HANDOFF_COMPILER` remains optional. Controller-generated Handoff copies the reviewed machine contract exactly.\n\n"
    },
